# Git hooks are executed by Git Bash on Windows and by /bin/sh on Linux.
# `pre-commit` and `pre-push` have no extension, so the repo-root `* text=auto`
# rule would check them out with CRLF on Windows and every run would die with
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# — a gate that is silently unable to start, which is the exact failure mode this
# directory exists to prevent. Force LF for everything in here, extension or not.
* text eol=lf
